x (BORC), it plays a role in the movement and localization of lysosomes at the cell periphery (PubMed:25898167, PubMed:38128568). Associated with the cytosolic face of lysosomes, BORC recruits ARL8B to the lysosomal membrane and couples lysosomes to microtubule plus-end-directed kinesin motors, driving lysosome movement toward the cell periphery."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}